nodecode-memoria is a rewrite of matrixorigin's matrixorigin/memoria:

  https://github.com/matrixorigin/memoria
  commit 3a5c5065b2820d56dd3d8ac8bb259a9424b1476e
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Matrix Origin (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the Hermes plugin under plugins/hermes — its REST client and its
error vocabulary, the six provider-owned tool schemas (memoria_search,
memoria_store, memoria_update, memoria_forget, memoria_profile,
memoria_feedback) and their per-argument bounds, the subject/session/branch
binding every request carries, the profile-home subject hash, the untrusted
recalled-context wrapper with its angle brackets escaped, the bounded
per-hit answers, the correction and deletion that read the exact record
before they touch it, feedback's main-branch rule, and the recall that rides
a turn's first round. All of it is reimplemented in Common Lisp against the
same HTTP API; no Python, and none of the original code, is bundled.

Left out, and why: the SQLite outbox, its claim tokens, backoff ladder and
uncertain-state receipts exist to make background turn *capture* survive a
crash and a restart, and this rewrite does no background capture at all —
Nodecode has no opt-in upload of completed turns, so there is nothing to
queue, deduplicate (`/v1/observe/deduplicated`) or recover. Also left out for
the same reason of scope: Hermes's `memory.write_approval` gate and its
gateway-platform exclusion (a Nodecode tool call is already the model's own
explicit act), the setup CLI and the diagnostics script (the section and
`/memoria` replace them), and the preview's host-specific tool-budget
arithmetic, replaced by a fixed per-memory bound.
